;; EXPECT: ok
;; DERIVE_AC_EQS: on
;; Book chapter 11: eager AC congruence closure.
;;
;; Same program as `11-cc-plain.egg`, one flag different. `--derive-ac-eqs` makes
;; every rebuild attempt AC completion, so the equality that plain mode misses is
;; in the graph by the time anything asks for it.
;;
;; What completion adds is the step plain recanonicalization cannot take: it treats
;; each asserted AC equation as a rewrite rule on multisets, and it closes that
;; rule set under the two operations that ground AC completion needs. Substituting
;; a known sub-sum into a node that contains it handles this file. Building the
;; superposition of two overlapping sums handles the harder case where the term
;; that exposes the equality is in no node at all.
;;
;; The price is that the closure is paid on EVERY rebuild, whether or not anything
;; needed it, and that it mints nodes: the substituted forms are real nodes that
;; stay in the graph.

(sort E)
(function add (E) E :assoc :comm)
(function a () E)
(function b () E)
(function c () E)
(function d () E)
(function n () E)

(union (add a b) c)
(union (add a b d) n)

(function f (E) E)
(check (= (f (add a b)) (f c)))

;; Derived, where plain mode failed.
(check (= n (add c d)))
